※ pl4g-test: module
※※ A module whose own lambda would be called what the importing file's is.
※
※ This is not a test of its own but a module the test beside it imports.  What
※ it is here for is that its lambda is the first one *it* writes, so the name
※ the compiler gives it is the name the other file's first lambda gets too.
@[export, impure]
fn run(x: u8) → u8:
    let f: fn(u8) → u8 = λ a: u8 → u8 { a + 1u8 }
    f(x)
